+# Safety & Certification Template — SRS + HARA (System Requirements & Hazard Analysis)
+
+This template is a working draft you must complete with project-specific details and evidence. Use it to prepare a safety case for external auditors.
+
+1) System Overview & Intended Use
+- System name: Aegis Autonomous AI Platform
+- Version: <version>
+- Operational Design Domain (ODD): define environment (indoor/outdoor), geography, payload, performance conditions, and assumptions.
+- Actors & users: operators, auditors, maintenance, end-users.
+
+2) System Requirements (SRS) — high level
+- Functional requirements:
+  - FR-1: The system shall accept multimodal inputs (image/audio/sensor) and produce model outputs for downstream agents.
+  - FR-2: The system shall enforce attestation-based access control for components that can actuate physical systems.
+  - FR-3: The system shall sign all production artifacts and evidence bundles using KMS-backed cosign keys.
+- Non-functional requirements:
+  - NFR-1: Latency requirements for closed-loop control < X ms.
+  - NFR-2: Availability for control plane > 99.9%.
+  - NFR-3: Audit retention: evidence retained for at least 365 days.
+
+3) Hazard Analysis and Risk Assessment (HARA)
+For each function that can lead to physical harm, enumerate:
+- Hazard ID: HZ-01
+  - Function: Agent issues movement command to robot
+  - Hazard: Unintended movement into human-occupied area
+  - Severity: High (injury potential)
+  - Likelihood: Possible
+  - Existing Mitigations:
+    - Hardware E-STOP
+    - ROS2 adapter geofence checks
+    - Attestation requirement for controller
+    - Argo remediation and automatic rollback on anomaly
+  - Residual risk: Acceptable with additional measures (runtime monitoring, mandatory HIL tests)
+  - Verification: HIL scenario ID HIL-MOVE-01 pass/fail record
+
+Repeat for all identified hazards (sensor failure, GPS spoofing, model hallucination, network partition).
+
+4) Safety Requirements Traceability Matrix (SRTM)
+- Map each requirement to hazards and tests:
+  - FR-2 -> HZ-01 -> Test: attestation_e2e_test.sh -> Evidence: /tmp/attest_evidence.json
+
+5) Test Plan & HIL scenarios
+- List HIL scenarios, inputs, expected outputs, pass/fail criteria, and artifacts collected.
+- Example: HIL-MOVE-01: navigate 5m in obstacle-free arena; pass if no geofence violations, max lateral error < 0.5m.
+
+6) Implementation & Verification
+- Describe implementation details for safety-critical components, including code references, Docker images, and builder provenance.
+- Verification steps: unit tests, integration tests, HIL runs, independent penetration tests.
+
+7) Operational Procedures & Runtime Controls
+- Describe operator procedures: emergency stop, override, multi-party approval flow, scheduled audits.
+- Define maintenance windows and rollback procedures.
+
+8) Evidence & Audit Artifacts
+- List of artifacts to provide to auditor: SBOMs, cosign signatures, Rekor entries, HIL logs, attestation logs, Terraform state snapshots, builder logs, test matrices.
+
+9) Certification plan & timeline
+- Identify target certifications (ISO 13482, ISO 26262, DO-178C if applicable) and plan milestones for external audits and remediation.
+
+10) Appendices
+- Glossary, acronyms, and references to standards/regulators.
+
